00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:49.340
Now, the data for CPI can be downloaded at
the second link on the screen, and it goes
back as far as 1947.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:05:05.000
And it's constructed by taking the
weighted averages of prices on a wide
variety of items, which are basically
assigned weights, representing their
importance within certain groups.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:22.460
And the prices are collected on a monthly
basis from 4,000 housing units and around
26,000 retail establishments across
cities, across 87 urban areas of the
United States.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:29.740
Now, this is obviously a large data set,
so it's a significant number.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:45.520
And of course, there's a lot of importance
placed on inflation by the Federal Reserve
in its dual mandate to maintain a certain
level of inflation and a target
employment.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:56.100
Now, this data set, obviously, it's a big
one, and this is because this is for the
CPI all items measure, okay?

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:05.580
So, 4,000 housing units and 26,000 retail
establishments across the 87 urban areas
of the U.S.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:14.360
But it's very important to remember, guys,
that CPI and inflation data in the U.S. is
a coincident indicator.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:20.300
It's telling us what is happening in the
economy now rather than in the future.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:28.340
So, it's not as useful as leading
indicators because the CPI follows our
leading indicators.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:36.080
By definition, inflation data is telling
us what happened to prices in the previous
month.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.640
However, it is useful to us.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.620
We do need to know, obviously, the level
of inflation in the economy.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:50.580
It's still useful as a confirmation
indicator because the Fed can be,
obviously, reactionary.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:58.160
And therefore, interest rate policy based
on inflation expectations can, obviously,
be affected.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:03.340
But always remember that it's a coincident
indicator.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:16.800
So, we use it as traders and portfolio
managers as a confirmation indicator to
essentially confirm what we were seeing in
the leading indicators in previous months.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.400
So, this is the all items number.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:22.900
So, this is including food and energy.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.440
So, links on the screen there.

