in which we analyzed the N2 money supply
data earlier in the PTM video series and
the various tradable instruments in the
IPLT video series.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:49.100
So, we calculate a distribution of returns
to discover what is a normal level of
inflation and what is an abnormal level of
inflation in order to assess future
monthly moves.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:14:15.020
So, we take the monthly index levels that
are reported by the BLS throughout history
and we work out percentage changes on a
month-by-month basis and then we run a
statistical distribution analysis.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:30.320
So, in the future, when we analyze any
inflation data releases, we can
distinguish between what is considered to
be a normal move and what is considered to
be an abnormal move for inflation.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:37.860
Now, you know how to use the method to
analyze data.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:56.260
So, if you have a self-starter mentality,
